{"id":"mahabharata-5-155","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":155,"title":"पञ्चपञ्चाशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 155 · Rukmin rejected by both sides","summary":{"en":"Rukmin, brother of Rukmini, comes with an army to help the Pandavas and boasts that he will defeat the Kurus single-handed if Arjuna is afraid. Arjuna, laughing, declines his help, and when Duryodhana too rejects him, Rukmin returns home.","kn":"ರುಕ್ಮಿಣಿಯ ಸಹೋದರ ರುಕ್ಮಿ ಪಾಂಡವರಿಗೆ ನೆರವಾಗಲು ಸೈನ್ಯದೊಂದಿಗೆ ಬಂದು ಅರ್ಜುನನು ಹೆದರಿದರೆ ತಾನೊಬ್ಬನೇ ಕುರುಗಳನ್ನು ಸೋಲಿಸುವೆನೆಂದು ಬಡಾಯಿ ಕೊಚ್ಚುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅರ್ಜುನನು ನಗುತ್ತಾ ಅವನ ಸಹಾಯ ನಿರಾಕರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನೂ ತಿರಸ್ಕರಿಸಿದಾಗ ರುಕ್ಮಿ ಮನೆಗೆ ಮರಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"रुक्मिणी का भाई रुक्मी सेना लेकर पाण्डवों की सहायता करने आता है और डींग मारता है कि यदि अर्जुन डरते हैं तो वह अकेला कुरुओं को हरा देगा। अर्जुन हँसकर उसकी सहायता अस्वीकार करते हैं, और जब दुर्योधन भी उसे ठुकराता है तो रुक्मी घर लौट जाता है।","te":"రుక్మిణి సోదరుడు రుక్మి పాండవులకు సహాయం చేయడానికి సైన్యంతో వచ్చి అర్జునుడు భయపడితే తానొక్కడే కురువులను ఓడిస్తానని గొప్పలు చెబుతాడు. అర్జునుడు నవ్వుతూ అతని సహాయాన్ని నిరాకరిస్తాడు; దుర్యోధనుడు కూడా తిరస్కరించగా రుక్మి ఇంటికి తిరిగివెళ్తాడు.","ta":"ருக்மிணியின் சகோதரன் ருக்மி படையுடன் பாண்டவர்களுக்கு உதவ வந்து, அர்ஜுனன் அஞ்சினால் தானே குருக்களைத் தனியே வெல்வேன் என்று வீம்பு பேசுகிறான். அர்ஜுனன் சிரித்தபடி அவன் உதவியை மறுக்க, துரியோதனனும் நிராகரித்ததும் ருக்மி வீடு திரும்புகிறான்.","ml":"രുക്മിണിയുടെ സഹോദരനായ രുക്മി സൈന്യവുമായി പാണ്ഡവരെ സഹായിക്കാനെത്തുന്നു; അർജുനൻ ഭയക്കുന്നുവെങ്കിൽ തനിച്ചുതന്നെ കുരുക്കളെ തോൽപ്പിക്കുമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം വീമ്പിളക്കുന്നു. ചിരിച്ചുകൊണ്ട് അർജുനൻ സഹായം നിരസിക്കുന്നു; ദുര്യോധനനും അതു നിരസിച്ചപ്പോൾ രുക്മി വീട്ടിലേക്ക് മടങ്ങുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.155; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"अभिनिर्याणपर्व","titleEn":"Abhiniryana Parva (The marching out)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एतस्मिन्नेव काले तु भीष्मकस्य महात्मनः ।\nहिरण्यलोम्नो नृपतेः साक्षादिन्द्रसखस्य वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"At this very time there was Rukmin, son of great-souled Bhishmaka, the golden-haired king who was a true friend of Indra,"}},{"n":2,"text":"आहृतीनामधिपतेर्भोजस्यातियशस्विनः ।\nदाक्षिणात्यपतेः पुत्रो दिक्षु रुक्मीति विश्रुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord of the Ahritis, the very famous king of the Bhojas and ruler of the south; Rukmin was renowned in all directions."}},{"n":3,"text":"यः किंपुरुषसिंहस्य गन्धमादनवासिनः ।\nशिष्यः कृत्स्नं धनुर्वेदं चतुष्पादमवाप्तवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He was the pupil of the lion among Kimpurushas who dwelt on Gandhamadana, and learned the whole four-part science of the bow."}},{"n":4,"text":"यो माहेन्द्रं धनुर्लेभे तुल्यं गाण्डीवतेजसा ।\nशार्ङ्गेण च महाबाहुः संमितं दिव्यमक्षयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That mighty-armed man obtained the bow of Mahendra, equal in power to Gandiva and to Sharnga, divine and unfailing."}},{"n":5,"text":"त्रीण्येवैतानि दिव्यानि धनूंषि दिविचारिणाम् ।\nवारुणं गाण्डिवं तत्र माहेन्द्रं विजयं धनुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There are just three divine bows of the dwellers in heaven: Varuna's Gandiva, and Mahendra's bow Vijaya."}},{"n":6,"text":"शार्ङ्गं तु वैष्णवं प्राहुर्दिव्यं तेजोमयं धनुः ।\nधारयामास यत्कृष्णः परसेनाभयावहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Sharnga is called Vishnu's divine bow made of radiance, which Krishna bore, a terror to enemy armies."}},{"n":7,"text":"गाण्डीवं पावकाल्लेभे खाण्डवे पाकशासनिः ।\nद्रुमाद्रुक्मी महातेजा विजयं प्रत्यपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Indra's son Arjuna got Gandiva from Agni at Khandava; the radiant Rukmin received Vijaya from Druma."}},{"n":8,"text":"संछिद्य मौरवान्पाशान्निहत्य मुरमोजसा ।\nनिर्जित्य नरकं भौममाहृत्य मणिकुण्डले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cutting the Mura nooses, killing Mura by force, defeating Naraka son of Earth, and bringing back the jeweled earrings,"}},{"n":9,"text":"षोडश स्त्रीसहस्राणि रत्नानि विविधानि च ।\nप्रतिपेदे हृषीकेशः शार्ङ्गं च धनुरुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hrishikesha took sixteen thousand women and many kinds of jewels, and also the excellent bow Sharnga."}},{"n":10,"text":"रुक्मी तु विजयं लब्ध्वा धनुर्मेघसमस्वनम् ।\nविभीषयन्निव जगत्पाण्डवानभ्यवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rukmin, having got Vijaya, a bow that thundered like clouds, came before the Pandavas as if frightening the world."}},{"n":11,"text":"नामृष्यत पुरा योऽसौ स्वबाहुबलदर्पितः ।\nरुक्मिण्या हरणं वीरो वासुदेवेन धीमता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long before, proud of the strength of his arms, he had not borne that wise Vasudeva carried off Rukmini."}},{"n":12,"text":"कृत्वा प्रतिज्ञां नाहत्वा निवर्तिष्यामि केशवम् ।\nततोऽन्वधावद्वार्ष्णेयं सर्वशस्त्रभृतां वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He vowed that he would not return without killing Keshava, and so chased the Vrishni, best of all weapon-bearers."}},{"n":13,"text":"सेनया चतुरङ्गिण्या महत्या दूरपातया ।\nविचित्रायुधवर्मिण्या गङ्गयेव प्रवृद्धया ॥","meaning":{"en":"He came with a great fourfold army that reached far, with varied weapons and armor, swollen like the Ganga."}},{"n":14,"text":"स समासाद्य वार्ष्णेयं योगानामीश्वरं प्रभुम् ।\nव्यंसितो व्रीडितो राजन्नाजगाम स कुण्डिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Meeting the Vrishni, lord of all yogas, he was humbled and ashamed, O king, and went to Kundina."}},{"n":15,"text":"यत्रैव कृष्णेन रणे निर्जितः परवीरहा ।\nतत्र भोजकटं नाम चक्रे नगरमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"On the very spot where Krishna had defeated that slayer of enemy heroes in battle, he built an excellent city called Bhojakata."}},{"n":16,"text":"सैन्येन महता तेन प्रभूतगजवाजिना ।\nपुरं तद्भुवि विख्यातं नाम्ना भोजकटं नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"With that great army with many elephants and horses, that city became known on earth by the name Bhojakata, O king."}},{"n":17,"text":"स भोजराजः सैन्येन महता परिवारितः ।\nअक्षौहिण्या महावीर्यः पाण्डवान्समुपागमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That king of the Bhojas, of great valor, surrounded by his great army of one akshauhini, came to the Pandavas."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततः स कवची खड्गी शरी धन्वी तली रथी ।\nध्वजेनादित्यवर्णेन प्रविवेश महाचमूम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, in armor, with sword, arrows, bow and gauntlet, in a chariot with a sun-colored banner, he entered the great army."}},{"n":19,"text":"विदितः पाण्डवेयानां वासुदेवप्रियेप्सया ।\nयुधिष्ठिरस्तु तं राजा प्रत्युद्गम्याभ्यपूजयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandavas knew him and, wishing to please Vasudeva, King Yudhishthira went to meet him and honored him."}},{"n":20,"text":"स पूजितः पाण्डुसुतैर्यथान्यायं सुसत्कृतः ।\nप्रतिपूज्य च तान्सर्वान्विश्रान्तः सहसैनिकः ।\nउवाच मध्ये वीराणां कुन्तीपुत्रं धनंजयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Honored by the sons of Pandu and well received, he honored them all in return, rested with his soldiers, and spoke to Arjuna son of Kunti in the midst of the heroes."}},{"n":21,"text":"सहायोऽस्मि स्थितो युद्धे यदि भीतोऽसि पाण्डव ।\nकरिष्यामि रणे साह्यमसह्यं तव शत्रुभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you are afraid, Pandava, I am here as your ally in the war; I will give you help in battle that your enemies cannot bear."}},{"n":22,"text":"न हि मे विक्रमे तुल्यः पुमानस्तीह कश्चन ।\nनिहत्य समरे शत्रूंस्तव दास्यामि फल्गुन ॥","meaning":{"en":"No man here equals me in prowess; I will kill your foes in battle and give you the victory, Phalguna."}},{"n":23,"text":"इत्युक्तो धर्मराजस्य केशवस्य च संनिधौ ।\nशृण्वतां पार्थिवेन्द्राणामन्येषां चैव सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So addressed, in the presence of Yudhishthira and Keshava, and while the other great kings all listened,"}},{"n":24,"text":"वासुदेवमभिप्रेक्ष्य धर्मराजं च पाण्डवम् ।\nउवाच धीमान्कौन्तेयः प्रहस्य सखिपूर्वकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna, son of Kunti, the wise, looked at Vasudeva and at Yudhishthira the Pandava, and laughed, speaking as to a friend."}},{"n":25,"text":"युध्यमानस्य मे वीर गन्धर्वैः सुमहाबलैः ।\nसहायो घोषयात्रायां कस्तदासीत्सखा मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"When I fought the mighty Gandharvas at the cattle-tour, who was my ally then? Who was my friend?"}},{"n":26,"text":"तथा प्रतिभये तस्मिन्देवदानवसंकुले ।\nखाण्डवे युध्यमानस्य कः सहायस्तदाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise in that fearsome battle at Khandava, thronged with gods and danavas, who helped me as I fought?"}},{"n":27,"text":"निवातकवचैर्युद्धे कालकेयैश्च दानवैः ।\nतत्र मे युध्यमानस्य कः सहायस्तदाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In war with the Nivatakavachas and the Kalakeya danavas, who helped me then as I fought?"}},{"n":28,"text":"तथा विराटनगरे कुरुभिः सह संगरे ।\nयुध्यतो बहुभिस्तात कः सहायोऽभवन्मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"And at Virata's city, when I fought many Kurus in battle, dear friend, who was my ally?"}},{"n":29,"text":"उपजीव्य रणे रुद्रं शक्रं वैश्रवणं यमम् ।\nवरुणं पावकं चैव कृपं द्रोणं च माधवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the war I relied on Rudra, Shakra, Kubera, Yama, Varuna, Agni, Kripa, Drona and Madhava."}},{"n":30,"text":"धारयन्गाण्डिवं दिव्यं धनुस्तेजोमयं दृढम् ।\nअक्षय्यशरसंयुक्तो दिव्यास्त्रपरिबृंहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I bear the divine Gandiva, a firm bow of radiance, with unfailing arrows, strengthened by divine weapons."}},{"n":31,"text":"कौरवाणां कुले जातः पाण्डोः पुत्रो विशेषतः ।\nद्रोणं व्यपदिशञ्शिष्यो वासुदेवसहायवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Born in the Kaurava family, a son of Pandu, calling Drona my teacher, and with Vasudeva as my helper,"}},{"n":32,"text":"कथमस्मद्विधो ब्रूयाद्भीतोऽस्मीत्ययशस्करम् ।\nवचनं नरशार्दूल वज्रायुधमपि स्वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"how could a man like me say, \"I am afraid,\" a shameful word, even to the thunderbolt-wielder himself, tiger among men?"}},{"n":33,"text":"नास्मि भीतो महाबाहो सहायार्थश्च नास्ति मे ।\nयथाकामं यथायोगं गच्छ वान्यत्र तिष्ठ वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am not afraid, mighty-armed one, and I have no need of an ally; go as you please and as suits you, or stay elsewhere."}},{"n":34,"text":"विनिवर्त्य ततो रुक्मी सेनां सागरसंनिभाम् ।\nदुर्योधनमुपागच्छत्तथैव भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Rukmin turned his ocean-like army away and went to Duryodhana in the same way, best of Bharatas."}},{"n":35,"text":"तथैव चाभिगम्यैनमुवाच स नराधिपः ।\nप्रत्याख्यातश्च तेनापि स तदा शूरमानिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise approaching him, that king spoke to him, but Duryodhana, proud of his heroism, rejected him too."}},{"n":36,"text":"द्वावेव तु महाराज तस्माद्युद्धाद्व्यपेयतुः ।\nरौहिणेयश्च वार्ष्णेयो रुक्मी च वसुधाधिपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Only two, great king, kept out of that war: Balarama son of Rohini, and Rukmin, lord of the earth."}},{"n":37,"text":"गते रामे तीर्थयात्रां भीष्मकस्य सुते तथा ।\nउपाविशन्पाण्डवेया मन्त्राय पुनरेव हि ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Rama had gone on pilgrimage and Bhishmaka's son had gone as well, the Pandavas sat down again to take counsel."}},{"n":38,"text":"समितिर्धर्मराजस्य सा पार्थिवसमाकुला ।\nशुशुभे तारकाचित्रा द्यौश्चन्द्रेणेव भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"That council of King Yudhishthira, crowded with kings, shone like the sky spangled with stars along with the moon, O Bharata."}}]}]}